WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.049
This fictional visit was recorded in
healthctl.

2
00:00:03.049 --> 00:00:04.706
Model waits are shortened.

3
00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.227
In New encounter, the user describes
something unusual.

4
00:00:08.227 --> 00:00:12.457
At choir practice, their own voice echoes
in their left ear.

5
00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:18.736
My own words first leaves room to describe
something the app hasn’t suggested.

6
00:00:19.150 --> 00:00:22.320
The app opens by asking how the symptom
has changed.

7
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:27.391
The user adds that humming a low note
brings on the echo, even alone in a

8
00:00:27.391 --> 00:00:28.025
quiet room.

9
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:35.408
The connected model asks, “Apart from the
echo, has it become harder to hear

10
00:00:35.408 --> 00:00:38.754
in your left ear?” This is the question
the user saw.

11
00:00:40.150 --> 00:00:42.691
The user can still hear people talking.

12
00:00:42.691 --> 00:00:46.683
It’s their own voice that sounds hollow,
especially after running to

13
00:00:46.683 --> 00:00:49.950
rehearsal. They type that distinction in
their own words.

14
00:00:52.150 --> 00:00:55.104
The model asks about the beginning of the
episode.

15
00:00:55.104 --> 00:00:59.698
Did other sounds suddenly get harder to
hear around the time the echo started?

16
00:01:01.150 --> 00:01:04.076
In history review, the user checks their
calendar.

17
00:01:04.076 --> 00:01:08.831
They change the timing to two rehearsals
ago, save the correction, and confirm

18
00:01:08.831 --> 00:01:09.563
the history.

19
00:01:10.150 --> 00:01:12.837
The clinician brief now includes the
corrected timing.

20
00:01:12.837 --> 00:01:16.867
The user can take this history to a
qualified healthcare professional to

21
00:01:16.867 --> 00:01:17.875
verify the findings.

22
00:01:18.150 --> 00:01:21.537
The user downloads the visit record from
the Report tab.
